        "title": "Injury, Rehabilitation, and Return-to-Play",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Sports injury rehabilitation is applied tissue biology constrained by competitive timelines. The framework: understand how tissue heals, what the clinical injury spectrum looks like, and how to progress loading to restore function without re-injury. Return-to-sport decision-making is a probability problem — the goal is not zero risk (impossible) but acceptable, quantified risk."
